        Chapter 1: Introduction                                         1-1









                             CHAPTER 1 - Introduction



        Under AOS/VS via the ?LOGC  system  call,  a  user  may  receive  a
        detailed log of all system calls issued either by or on  behalf  of
        the calling process.  Under AOS/VS, all system calls go through the
        system, including task calls, resource calls, etc.   The  log  pro-
        duced by ?LOGC may also include system calls made by the system  on
        behalf of a user system request (e.g., a ?SEND causes the system to
        use the IPC mechanism to transfer the message to the target).   The
        log produced by this call is written to disk  in  a  pre-determined
        format.

        The LOGCALLS utility is  designed  to  read  this  logfile  and  to
        generate a report  file  containing  the  interpreted  ?LOGC  data.
        Through the specification of user-defined  parameters,  the  report
        may be tailored to the user's needs.

             LOGCALLS support includes the following:

              * Support for 16-bit and 32-bit processes.

              * For each system call issued, a  summary  report  indicating
                the frequency of call issuance from each of rings 3, 4,  5,
                6, and 7.  Totals for all calls are provided.

              * Mnemonic representations of all system calls.

              * Full user-ring support.  User rings 4, 5, 6, and 7 are  all
                fully supported.


             LOGCALLS optionally provides the following:

              * A report detailing the calls issued by all tasks.

              * Reports detailing the calls issued by each task.

              * A report detailing the calls issued by a particular task.

              * Symbolic representations for  all  logical  addresses  from
                which the system calls were issued.

              * Full ring 3 (AGENT) support.  System calls  issued  by  the
                AGENT on behalf of the user will be reported.



        Data General Corporation                       Company Confidential
                LOGCALLS - System Call Logging Utility, Rev. 1               Page 2
        Chapter 1: Introduction                                         1-2



        The generated report file consists of a report header followed by a
        chart of all system calls in chronological  order  of  issue.   For
        each system call, this chart supplies the system call mnemonic  and
        octal representation, the accumulator values (AC0,AC1  &  AC2)  and
        program counter at system call issuance, the task ID  and  the  TCB
        number (indicating the order in which the tasks were  initialized).
        By user  request,  the  symbolic  representations  of  all  program
        counters can also be provided.



                                 [End of Chapter 1]











































