        Chapter 3: Output Format                                        3-1









                             CHAPTER 3 - Output Format



        LOGCALLS produces a report file consisting of a  header,  a  system
        call summary chart, and a report or reports for each of  the  /ALL,
        /EACH and  /TASK=  switches  selected.   These  three  modules  are
        described in more detail below.

        ______        Header

        The header contains the following information:

        	+   Target Process name
        	+   Target Program pathname
        	+   Ring 7 Symbol File name  (if specified)
        	+   Ring 6 Symbol File name  (if specified)
        	+   Ring 5 Symbol File name  (if specified)
        	+   Ring 4 Symbol File name  (if specified)
        	+   Ring 3 Symbol File name  (if specified)
        	+   Date/Time of ?LOGC initialization

        ______________        Summary Report

        The summary report of system calls is analyzed by system  call  and
        by protection ring, and contains the following information for each
        call issued:

        	+   System call mnemonic
        	+   System call octal value
        	+   Count of system call issued in Ring 3
        	+   Count of system call issued in Ring 4
        	+   Count of system call issued in Ring 5
        	+   Count of system call issued in Ring 6
        	+   Count of system call issued in Ring 7
        	+   Total count of system call issued from all rings

        The following information on all calls is also provided:

        	+   Total system calls issued from Ring 3
        	+   Total system calls issued from Ring 4
        	+   Total system calls issued from Ring 5
        	+   Total system calls issued from Ring 6
        	+   Total system calls issued from Ring 7
        	+   Total system calls issued from all rings




        Data General Corporation                       Company Confidential
                LOGCALLS - System Call Logging Utility, Rev. 1               Page 7
        Chapter 3: Output Format                                        3-2



        __________________        Detailed Report(s)

        Detailed information concerning each  system  call  issued  may  be
        requested by specifying  the  optional  switches  /ALL,  /EACH,  or
        /TASK=.  The system calls are listed in chronological order of time
        of issuance.  For  each  issuance,  the  following  information  is
        provided:

        	+   System call mnemonic
        	+   System call octal value
        	+   Accumulator 0 value @ call issuance
        	+   Accumulator 1 value @ call issuance
        	+   Accumulator 2 value @ call issuance
        	+   Program Counter     @ call issuance
        	+   Task ID of task issuing call
        	+   TCB number (indicating order of task initialization)
        	+   Symbolic representation of the Program Counter (optional)



                                 [End of Chapter 3]


































        Data General Corporation                       Company Confidential
